<span class="craft-v2-concept">AI-generated conceptual visual</span><div class="craft-v2-hero-inner"><div><p class="craft-v2-eyebrow">Field journal · Process</p><h1>{{title}}</h1></div><div><p class="craft-v2-dek">{{#if custom_excerpt}}{{custom_excerpt}}{{else}}Between a green capsule and a stable dried spice lies the question DHUNERI is here to investigate.{{/if}}</p><p class="craft-v2-meta">Tradition · adaptation · laboratory evidence</p></div></div></section><section class="craft-v2-opening"><div class="craft-v2-wrap craft-v2-opening-grid craft-v2-reveal"><div><p class="craft-v2-eyebrow">Entry 01 · The problem</p><h2>Drying is not a <em>footnote.</em></h2></div><div class="craft-v2-opening-copy"><p class="craft-v2-lead">It is the stage where heat, smoke, airflow, time and judgment meet—and where quality can be preserved or lost.</p><p>Traditional knowledge defines the starting point. Controlled alternatives create testable possibilities. We document both without treating an inherited method as backward or a new machine as automatically better.</p><p class="craft-v2-question">Research principle: compare methods under documented conditions, then let measurements—not visual preference—shape the conclusion.</p></div></div></section><section class="craft-v2-journey"><div class="craft-v2-wrap"><div class="craft-v2-journey-head craft-v2-reveal"><div><p class="craft-v2-eyebrow">Process map</p><h2>One batch, <em>five moments.</em></h2></div><p>The page follows the capsule from the field to a result that can be examined, repeated and discussed.</p></div><div class="craft-v2-steps craft-v2-reveal"><article><b>i.</b><h3>Harvest</h3><p>Record maturity, date, location and handling.</p></article><article><b>ii.</b><h3>Move</h3><p>Track time and conditions before drying begins.</p></article><article><b>iii.</b><h3>Dry</h3><p>Observe heat, smoke, airflow, fuel and duration.</p></article><article><b>iv.</b><h3>Condition</h3><p>Allow the dried batch to stabilise before testing.</p></article><article><b>v.</b><h3>Test</h3><p>Measure what the method changed—and what it did not.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="craft-v2-fresh"><div class="craft-v2-fresh-image"><span>AI-generated conceptual visual</span></div><div class="craft-v2-fresh-copy craft-v2-reveal"><p class="craft-v2-eyebrow">Entry 02 · Starting material</p><h2>Before the <em>fire.</em></h2><p>A comparison is meaningful only when the starting material is documented. Harvest maturity, initial moisture, elapsed time and batch mass belong beside every drying result.</p><div class="craft-v2-log"><div><b>01</b><span>Harvest context</span></div><div><b>02</b><span>Initial moisture</span></div><div><b>03</b><span>Elapsed time</span></div><div><b>04</b><span>Batch mass</span></div></div></div></section><section class="craft-v2-methods"><div class="craft-v2-wrap"><div class="craft-v2-reveal"><p class="craft-v2-eyebrow">Entry 03 · Methods</p><h2>Four ways to ask the <em>same question.</em></h2><p class="craft-v2-intro">Select a method to see its role in the comparison. These are research directions, not claims about performance.</p></div><div class="craft-v2-method-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Drying methods"><button id="craft-tab-bhatti" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="craft-method-panel" tabindex="0" data-title="Traditional bhatti" data-copy="The baseline method to document: hearth structure, fuel, loading pattern, temperature variation, smoke exposure and operator decisions." data-state="Baseline to document" data-image="bhatti">Traditional bhatti</button><button id="craft-tab-improved" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="craft-method-panel" tabindex="-1" data-title="Improved bhatti" data-copy="A modified combustion and airflow path may reduce direct smoke exposure while retaining locally available fuel and familiar operation." data-state="Candidate method" data-image="bhatti">Improved bhatti</button><button id="craft-tab-air" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="craft-method-panel" tabindex="-1" data-title="Controlled hot air" data-copy="A measured temperature and airflow profile creates a repeatable comparison, but practicality, energy and cost must be included." data-state="Candidate method" data-image="alternative">Controlled hot air</button><button id="craft-tab-solar" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="craft-method-panel" tabindex="-1" data-title="Solar-assisted hybrid" data-copy="Solar heat may reduce fuel or electricity demand, while backup heat can protect the process during variable weather." data-state="Candidate method" data-image="alternative">Solar hybrid</button></div><article id="craft-method-panel" class="craft-v2-method-card craft-v2-reveal" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="craft-tab-bhatti"><div class="craft-v2-method-visual" data-craft-method-image="bhatti"><span>AI-generated conceptual visual</span></div><div class="craft-v2-method-copy"><span id="craft-method-state">Baseline to document</span><h3 id="craft-method-title">Traditional bhatti</h3><p id="craft-method-copy">The baseline method to document: hearth structure, fuel, loading pattern, temperature variation, smoke exposure and operator decisions.</p><small>No comparative result claimed</small></div></article></div></section>
